ADAM Instruction Manual — licence
=================================

This repository holds two different kinds of work, and each carries its own
licence.


The documentation
-----------------

Everything under `docs/` — the prose, the screenshots and the other images —
is:

    Copyright (c) 2026 ADAM EduTech

and is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike
4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).

You are free to copy, redistribute and adapt the manual, provided that:

  * Attribution — you credit ADAM EduTech, link back to
    https://help.adam.co.za/, and state whether you changed anything.

  * NonCommercial — you do not use it for a commercial purpose, meaning one
    primarily intended for commercial advantage or monetary compensation.
    Selling printed copies, charging for access, and folding it into a paid
    product or service all fall under this.

  * ShareAlike — if you adapt it, you release what you make under this same
    licence.

The three paragraphs above are a summary, not the licence. The licence is the
full legal text in `LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt`, and that text governs if the
two ever appear to differ. Creative Commons publishes its own plain-language
summary at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/


The site machinery
------------------

The files that build, style and publish the site — `theme/`, `hooks/`,
`scripts/`, `bin/`, `pdf/`, `mkdocs.yml` and `mkdocs.pdf.yml`, but not the
third-party packages under any `node_modules/` directory, which carry their own
licences — are:

    Copyright (c) 2026 ADAM EduTech

and are licensed under the MIT licence, whose text is in `LICENSES/MIT.txt`.
Reuse them for anything at all, commercial or not. They are licensed separately
so that nobody has to reason about the manual's terms in order to borrow a
build hook.


Trade marks
-----------

Neither licence grants any right in the name ADAM, the name ADAM EduTech, or
the ADAM logo (`theme/img/logo.png`). A copy or adaptation of this manual may
not be presented in a way that suggests it is the official ADAM documentation,
or that ADAM EduTech endorses it.


Text and data mining
--------------------

ADAM EduTech expressly reserves all rights to carry out text and data mining of
this manual, including any use of it to train, fine-tune or ground a
machine-learning model, and including retrieval from a stored index or
embedding of its contents.

This is a machine-readable reservation of rights for the purposes of Article
4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790 and of equivalent provisions elsewhere. The
licences above grant no permission for such use.


Something commercial in mind?
